# Process Charter: IT Change Management

## 1. Process Objective
Enhance IT operational stability and minimize business disruption (unplanned downtime) by evaluating, approving, and executing infrastructure and application changes in a structured manner.

## 2. Process Scope
* **In Scope:** All changes to Hardware, Network, Servers, Software, Databases, and Cloud Infrastructure in Production environments.
* **Out of Scope:** Standard user service requests (handled via Service Request Management).

## 3. RACI Matrix
| Role / Function | Request Creation | CAB Review & Risk Assessment | Execution | Post-Implementation Review (PIR) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Change Requester** | **R** (Responsible) | **I** (Informed) | **I** (Informed) | **C** (Consulted) |
| **Change Advisory Board (CAB)** | **I** (Informed) | **A** (Accountable) | **I** (Informed) | **A** (Accountable) |
| **Infrastructure / Dev Team** | **C** (Consulted) | **C** (Consulted) | **R** (Responsible) | **R** (Responsible) |

## 4. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
* **Success Rate of Changes:** ≥ 98%
* **Emergency Change Ratio:** < 5% of total Change Requests
* **Unplanned Outages Caused by Changes:** 0 Incidents (Target)
